.\n\nAs operating systems and GUIs have moved on to scalable vector fonts, the bitmap fonts that dominated\nthe 1980s and 1990s languish away in non-obvious and often binary formats that are rapidly falling\ninto obscurity.\n\nThe main purpose of this repository is to liberate these fonts from their binary shackles,\npreserving the ancient art of monochrome bitmap typography for human appreciation.\n\nThe fonts in this repository are stored in [the human-friendly text-based YAFF format](https://github.com/robhagemans/monobit/blob/master/YAFF.md).\nAs such, the easiest way to view them is to open the text files directly. Alternatively, you can use\n[`monobit`](https://github.com/robhagemans/monobit) to render them to images or convert them to\nfont formats supported by current operating systems. You can also\n[see the fonts as images here](http://robhagemans.github.io/monobit/).\n"}],"copyright":"","sourceLicense":""},"source":{"collection":"hoard","recordId":"hoard-geos-bsw-bold-c128","revision":"d11f085795149f7d246d365abd98b91d56b0789d","sha256":"6f53b5bcc832795d9a051cdc4b4474fe09e670be7fd315d488f7082e5ca1da95","upstream":{"name":"Hoard of Bitfonts","url":"https://github.com/robhagemans/hoard-of-bitfonts/blob/d11f085795149f7d246d365abd98b91d56b0789d/geos/bsw-bold-c128.yaff","collectionUrl":"https://github.com/robhagemans/hoard-of-bitfonts/","author":"Rob Hagemans","retrievedAt":"2026-07-21","revision":"d11f085795149f7d246d365abd98b91d56b0789d","file":"geos/bsw-bold-c128.yaff","fileSha256":"6f53b5bcc832795d9a051cdc4b4474fe09e670be7fd315d488f7082e5ca1da95","packIndex":0}},"provenance":{"decoder":"monobit 0.52.0","nativeGlyphs":95,"packIndex":0,"sourceHeader":"","rasterSha256":"eaca97a64111a5e934916e5f3c308b8c78742933dd32aa26505898eac4387770","transformation":"Native glyph rasters and metrics; no resizing, thresholding or invented Unicode labels."},"modifications":[],"coverage":{"glyphCount":95,"unicodeGlyphCount":0,"unmappedGlyphCount":95,"ukrainian":{"required":66,"